{"timestamp":"2026-11-14T20:41:25.999Z","ordinal":296,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1dbcb-24ef-75a0-a30a-5f6b74ba04a6","call_id":"call_f30c5d1454ff45ac8fdeeeebdb4762aa","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 7.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"8b5b43\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.2653829,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":433,\"output\":\"thread_history_1.sqlite\\r\\n_sqlx_migrations CREATE TABLE _sqlx_migrations (\\r\\n    version BIGINT PRIMARY KEY,\\r\\n    description TEXT NOT NULL,\\r\\n    installed_on TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\\r\\n    success BOOLEAN NOT NULL,\\r\\n    checksum BLOB NOT NULL,\\r\\n    execution_time BIGINT NOT NULL\\r\\n)\\r\\nthread_turns CREATE TABLE thread_turns (\\r\\r\\n    thread_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    turn_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    rollout_ordinal INTEGER NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    status TEXT NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    error_json TEXT,\\r\\r\\n    started_at INTEGER,\\r\\r\\n    completed_at INTEGER,\\r\\r\\n    duration_ms INTEGER,\\r\\r\\n    first_user_item_id TEXT,\\r\\r\\n    final_agent_item_id TEXT, rollout_byte_offset INTEGER, rollout_end_ordinal INTEGER, rollout_end_byte_offset INTEGER, root_turn_id TEXT,\\r\\r\\n    PRIMARY KEY (thread_id, turn_id)\\r\\r\\n)\\r\\nthread_items CREATE TABLE thread_items (\\r\\r\\n    thread_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    turn_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    item_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    rollout_ordinal INTEGER NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    created_at_ms INTEGER NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    item_json TEXT NOT NULL, item_type TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '', updated_at_ordinal INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, started_at_ms INTEGER, completed_at_ms INTEGER,\\r\\r\\n    PRIMARY KEY (thread_id, turn_id, item_id)\\r\\r\\n)\\r\\nthread_history_projection_state CREATE TABLE thread_history_projection_state (\\r\\r\\n    thread_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\\r\\r\\n    next_rollout_byte_offset INTEGER NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    next_rollout_ordinal INTEGER NOT NULL\\r\\r\\n)\\r\\nthread_realtime_items CREATE TABLE thread_realtime_items (\\r\\r\\n    thread_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    item_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    rollout_ordinal INTEGER NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    created_at_ms INTEGER NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    item_type TEXT NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    item_json TEXT NOT NULL,\\r\\r\\n    PRIMARY KEY (thread_id, item_id)\\r\\r\\n)\\r\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Developer commands | ChatGPT Learn (https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/developer-commands?surface=cli ; rewritten summary of https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/developer-commands?surface=cli)\nciteturn4view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view0\",\"pattern\":\"Resume a previous\"}); Redirected to URL: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/developer-commands?surface=cli; Total lines: 4110\nL1292: 【575†`codex features`】  | Stable  | List feature flags and persistently enable or disable them in `config.toml`.\nL1293: 【576†`codex fork`】  | Stable  | Fork a previous interactive session into a new chat, preserving the original transcript.\nL1294: 【577†`codex login`】  | Stable  | Authenticate Codex using ChatGPT OAuth, device auth, an API key, or an access token piped over stdin.\nL1295: 【578†`codex logout`】  | Stable  | Remove stored authentication credentials.\nL1296: 【579†`codex mcp`】  | Stable  | Manage Model Context Protocol servers (list, add, remove, authenticate).\nL1297: 【580†`codex plugin`】  | Stable  | Install, list, and remove plugins from configured marketplace sources.\nL1298: 【581†`codex plugin marketplace`】  | Stable  | Add, list, upgrade, or remove plugin marketplaces from Git or local sources.\nL1299: 【582†`codex queue`】  | Stable  | Queue a text message for an existing session by UUID or exact name.\nL1300: 【583†`codex remote-control`】  | Experimental  | Run or manage remote control for the local app-server, or create a short-lived pairing code.\nL1301: 【584†`codex resume`】  | Stable  | Continue a previous interactive session by ID or resume the most recent chat.\nL1302: 【585†`codex review`】  | Stable  | Run a non-interactive review of uncommitted changes, a base branch diff, a commit, or custom review instructions.\nL1303: 【586†`codex sandbox`】  | Stable  | Run arbitrary commands inside Codex-provided macOS, Linux, or Windows sandboxes.\nL1304: 【565†`codex unarchive`】  | Stable  | Restore an archived interactive session by session ID or session name.\nL1305: 【587†`codex update`】  | Stable  | Check for and apply a Codex CLI update when the installed release supports self-update.\nL1306: Key\nL1307: \nL1308: 【560†`codex`】\nL1309: \nL1310: Maturity\nL1311: \nL1312: Stable\nL1313: \nL1314: Details\nL1315: \nL1316: Launch the terminal UI. Accepts the global flags above plus an optional prompt or image attachments.\nL1317: \nL1318: Key\nL1319: \nL1320: 【561†`codex agents`】\nL1321: \nL1322: Maturity\nL1323: \nL1324: Stable\nL1325: \nL1326: Details\nL1327: \nL1328: Open the agent command center on a shared local or remote server.\nL1329: \nL1330: Key\nL1331: \nL1332: 【562†`codex app`】\nL1333: \nL1334: Maturity\nL1335: \nL1336: Stable\nL1337: \nL1338: Details\nL1339: \nL1340: Launch the ChatGPT desktop app on macOS or Windows. On macOS, Codex can open a workspace path; on Windows, Codex prints the path to open.\nL1341: \nL1342: Key\nL1343: \nL1344: 【563†`codex app-server`】\nL1345: \nL1346: Maturity\nL1347: Experimental\nL1348: \nL1349: Details\nL1350: \nL1351: Launch the Codex app server for local development or debugging over stdio, WebSocket, or a Unix socket.\nL1352: \nL1353: Key\nL1354: \nL1355: 【564†`codex apply`】\nL1356: \nL1357: Maturity\nL1358: \nL1359: Stable\nL1360: \nL1361: Details\nL1362: \nL1363: Apply the latest diff generated by a Codex cloud chat to your local working tree. Alias: `codex a`.\nL1364: \nL1365: Key\nL1366: \nL1456: Generate a diagnostic report for local installation, config, auth, runtime, Git, terminal, app-server, and thread inventory issues.\nL1457: \nL1458: Key\nL1459: \nL1460: 【573†`codex exec`】\nL1461: \nL1462: Maturity\nL1463: \nL1464: Stable\nL1465: \nL1466: Details\nL1467: \nL1468: Run Codex non-interactively. Alias: `codex e`. Stream results to stdout or JSONL, resume sessions, or fork them into new sessions.\nL1469: \nL1470: Key\nL1471: \nL1472: 【574†`codex execpolicy`】\nL1473: \nL1474: Maturity\nL1475: \nL1476: Experimental\nL1477: \nL1478: Details\nL1479: \nL1480: Evaluate execpolicy rule files and see whether a command would be allowed, prompted, or blocked.\nL1481: \nL1482: Key\nL1483: \nL1484: 【575†`codex features`】\nL1485: Maturity\nL1486: \nL1487: Stable\nL1488: \nL1489: Details\nL1490: \nL1491: List feature flags and persistently enable or disable them in `config.toml`.\nL1492: \nL1493: Key\nL1494: \nL1495: 【576†`codex fork`】\nL1496: \nL1497: Maturity\nL1498: \nL1499: Stable\nL1500: \nL1501: Details\nL1502: \nL1503: Fork a previous interactive session into a new chat, preserving the original transcript.\nL1504: \nL1505: Key\nL1506: \nL1507: 【577†`codex login`】\nL1508: \nL1509: Maturity\nL1510: \nL1511: Stable\nL1512: \nL1513: Details\nL1514: \nL1515: Authenticate Codex using ChatGPT OAuth, device auth, an API key, or an access token piped over stdin.\nL1516: \nL1517: Key\nL1518: \nL1519: 【578†`codex logout`】\nL1520: \nL1521: Maturity\nL1522: \nL1523: Stable\nL1524: \nL1525: Details\nL1526: \nL1527: Remove stored authentication credentials.\nL1528: \nL1529: Key\nL1530: 【579†`codex mcp`】\nL1531: \nL1532: Maturity\nL1533: \nL1534: Stable\nL1535: \nL1536: Details\nL1537: \nL1538: Manage Model Context Protocol servers (list, add, remove, authenticate).\nL1539: \nL1540: Key\nL1541: \nL1542: 【580†`codex plugin`】\nL1543: \nL1544: Maturity\nL1545: \nL1546: Stable\nL1547: \nL1548: Details\nL1549: \nL1550: Install, list, and remove plugins from configured marketplace sources.\nL1551: \nL1552: Key\nL1553: \nL1554: 【581†`codex plugin marketplace`】\nL1555: \nL1556: Maturity\nL1557: \nL1558: Stable\nL1559: \nL1560: Details\nL1561: \nL1562: Add, list, upgrade, or remove plugin marketplaces from Git or local sources.\nL1563: \nL1564: Key\nL1565: \nL1566: 【582†`codex queue`】\nL1567: \nL1568: Maturity\nL1569: \nL1570: Stable\nL1571: \nL1572: Details\nL1573: \nL1574: Queue a text message for an existing session by UUID or exact name.\nL1575: Key\nL1576: \nL1577: 【583†`codex remote-control`】\nL1578: \nL1579: Maturity\nL1580: \nL1581: Experimental\nL1582: \nL1583: Details\nL1584: \nL1585: Run or manage remote control for the local app-server, or create a short-lived pairing code.\nL1586: \nL1587: Key\nL1588: \nL1589: 【584†`codex resume`】\nL1590: \nL1591: Maturity\nL1592: \nL1593: Stable\nL1594: \nL1595: Details\nL1596: \nL1597: Continue a previous interactive session by ID or resume the most recent chat.\nL1598: \nL1599: Key\nL1600: \nL1601: 【585†`codex review`】\nL1602: \nL1603: Maturity\nL1604: \nL1605: Stable\nL1606: \nL1607: Details\nL1608: \nL1609: Run a non-interactive review of uncommitted changes, a base branch diff, a commit, or custom review instructions.\nL1610: \nL1611: Key\nL1612: \nL1613: 【586†`codex sandbox`】\nL1614: \nL1615: Maturity\nL1616: \nL1617: Stable\nL1618: Details\nL1619: \nL1620: Run arbitrary commands inside Codex-provided macOS, Linux, or Windows sandboxes.\nL1621: \nL1622: Key\nL1623: \nL1624: 【565†`codex unarchive`】\nL1625: \nL1626: Maturity\nL1627: \nL1628: Stable\nL1629: \nL1630: Details\nL1631: \nL1632: Restore an archived interactive session by session ID or session name.\nL1633: \nL1634: Key\nL1635: \nL1636: 【587†`codex update`】\nL1637: \nL1638: Maturity\nL1639: \nL1640: Stable\nL1641: \nL1642: Details\nL1643: \nL1644: Check for and apply a Codex CLI update when the installed release supports self-update.\nL1645: \nL1646: [Button: Expand to view all]\nL1647: ## Command details\nL1648: ### `codex` (interactive)\nL1649: \nL1650: Running `codex` with no subcommand launches the interactive terminal UI (TUI). The agent accepts the global flags above plus image attachments. Web search defaults to cached mode; use `--search` to switch to live browsing. For low-friction local work, use `--sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval on-request`.\nL2194: #### `codex cloud list`\nL2195: \nL2196: List recent cloud chats with optional filtering and pagination.\nL2197: \nL2198: [Input: Filter by key, type, or details]\nL2199: \nL2200: Key  | Type / Values  | Details\nL2201: --- | --- | ---\nL2202: `--cursor`  | `string`  | Pagination cursor returned by a previous request.\nL2203: `--env`  | `ENV_ID`  | Filter tasks by environment identifier.\nL2204: `--json`  | `boolean`  | Emit machine-readable JSON instead of plain text.\nL2205: `--limit`  | `1-20`  | Maximum number of tasks to return.\nL2206: \nL2207: Key\nL2208: \nL2209: `--cursor`\nL2210: \nL2211: Type / Values\nL2212: \nL2213: `string`\nL2214: \nL2215: Details\nL2216: Pagination cursor returned by a previous request.\nL2217: \nL2218: Key\nL2219: \nL2220: `--env`\nL2221: \nL2222: Type / Values\nL2223: \nL2224: `ENV_ID`\nL2225: \nL2226: Details\nL2227: \nL2228: Filter tasks by environment identifier.\nL2229: \nL2230: Key\nL2231: \nL2232: `--json`\nL2233: \nL2234: Type / Values\nL2235: \nL2236: `boolean`\nL2237: \nL2238: Details\nL2239: \nL2240: Emit machine-readable JSON instead of plain text.\nL2241: \nL2242: Key\nL2243: \nL2244: `--limit`\nL2245: \nL2246: Type / Values\nL2247: \nL2248: `1-20`\nL2249: \nL2250: Details\nL2251: \nL2252: Maximum number of tasks to return.\nL2253: Plain-text output prints a task URL followed by status details. Use `--json` for automation. The JSON payload contains a `tasks` array plus an optional `cursor` value. Each task includes `id`, `url`, `title`, `status`, `updated_at`, `environment_id`, `environment_label`, `summary`, `is_review`, and `attempt_total`.\nL2254: ### `codex completion`\nL2255: \nL2256: Generate shell completion scripts and redirect the output to the appropriate location, for example `codex completion zsh > \"${fpath[1]}/_codex\"`.\nL2257: \nL2258: [Input: Filter by key, type, or details]\nL2259: \nL2260: Key  | Type / Values  | Details\nL2261: --- | --- | ---\nL2262: `SHELL`  | `bash | zsh | fish | power-shell | elvish`  | Shell to generate completions for. Output prints to stdout.\nL2263: \nL2264: Key\nL2265: \nL2266: `SHELL`\nL2267: \nL2268: Type / Values\nL2269: \nL2270: `bash | zsh | fish | power-shell | elvish`\nL2271: \nL2272: Details\nL3233: ### `codex fork`\nL3234: \nL3235: Fork a previous interactive session into a new chat. By default, `codex fork` opens the session picker. Use `--last` to fork the most recent session in the current directory. Use `--last --all` to fork the most recent session across all directories.\nL3236: \nL3237: When the current and saved session directories differ, `codex fork` uses the same working-directory prompt and `tui.resume_cwd` setting as `codex resume`.\nL3238: \nL3239: [Input: Filter by key, type, or details]\nL3633: 【630†`/resume`】  | Resume a saved chat from your session list.  | Continue work from a previous CLI session without starting over.\nL3634: 【631†`/new`】  | Start a new chat inside the same CLI session.  | Reset the chat context without leaving the CLI when you want a fresh prompt in the same repo.\nL3635: 【606†`/quit`】  | Exit the CLI.  | Leave the session immediately.\nL3636: 【632†`/review`】  | Ask Codex to review your working tree.  | Run after Codex completes work or when you want a second set of eyes on local changes.\nL3637: 【633†`/status`】  | Display session configuration and token usage.  | Confirm the active model, approval policy, writable roots, and remaining context capacity.\nL3638: 【634†`/usage`】  | View account token usage or use a rate-limit reset.  | Inspect daily, weekly, or cumulative ChatGPT token activity from inside the TUI.\nL3639: 【635†`/debug-config`】  | Print config layer and requirements diagnostics.  | Debug precedence and policy requirements, including experimental network constraints.\nL3955: ### Resume a saved chat with `/resume`\nL3956: \nL3957:   1. Type `/resume` and press Enter.\nL3958:   2. Choose a search scope in the picker. `Cwd` shows chats from the current directory. `Repo`, when available, includes the corresponding directory in linked local worktrees. `All` searches across directories.\nL3959:   3. Select the chat you want to resume.\nL3960: \nL3961: Expected: Codex reloads the selected chat’s transcript so you can pick up where you left off, keeping the original history intact.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDeveloper commands | ChatGPT Learn (https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/developer-commands?surface=cli ; rewritten summary of https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/developer-commands?surface=cli)\nciteturn4view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view0\",\"pattern\":\".codex/sessions\"}); Redirected to URL: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/developer-commands?surface=cli; Total lines: 4110\nNo matching text found for \".codex/sessions\""}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1dbc1-59c0-7a41-a30f-7c85c2fa1732","create_time":1794688885.9991674}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
